# No agent prefixes in git or messages

Never use `cursor/` (or similar agent/tool prefixes) in branch names, commit messages, pull request titles/bodies, or user-facing chat.

```text
# ❌ BAD
cursor/add-screen-record
cursor/fix-hyprland-binds

# ✅ GOOD
add-screen-record
fix-hyprland-binds
```

Follow the repo's existing branch naming if it already has a convention (e.g. `feat/...`). Still do not add a `cursor/` prefix on top of that.

Do not mention `cursor/` in commit messages, PR titles, PR descriptions, or similar git metadata. Describe the change, not the tool that made it.
